          "text": "Nicotine withdrawal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "When cutting down smoking, reports irritability, anxiety, decreased concentration, and being snappy. Previous cold-turkey quit attempt lasted approximately one week and was followed by relapse with irritability and poor sleep. Nicotine patch alone approximately five years ago helped somewhat, but cravings persisted."
